<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Bergamo</h1><p class="st-meta">1797 CE – 1797 CE · capital Bergamo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A republic proclaimed when Bergamo rose against Venetian rule with French backing in March 1797, before joining the Cisalpine Republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-bergamo">Bergamo</a> had been a mainland city of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a> since 1428. In March 1797, with French troops in the city, local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobin-club">Jacobins</a> proclaimed Bergamo's independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and set up a provisional government.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Bergamasque Republic was a provisional regime of local patriots under French protection. It abolished Venetian institutions, planted liberty trees and sought union with the new republics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>. Its revolt helped trigger risings in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-brescia">Brescia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crema">Crema</a>, which weakened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in the last weeks before its fall.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> fell in May 1797, and later that year <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-bergamo">Bergamo</a> was united to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cisalpine-republic">Cisalpine Republic</a>, created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1797 CE – 1797 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:95.46%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1797 CE – 1797 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bergamo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombard, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bergamasque Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1797&amp;focus=republic-of-bergamo" aria-label="Republic of Bergamo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4909 567 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Bergamo lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5229 823L5293 831M5229 823L5218 830"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5293 831h0M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5229 823h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5229 823h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bergamo. <a href="/atlas?year=1797&amp;focus=republic-of-bergamo">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
